{"name":"Dancing Jewel","hex":"#429b77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dancing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The activity of taking part in a dance.","A dance club in France."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of dance"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancing"},{"term":"jewel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A precious or semi-precious stone; gem, gemstone.","A valuable object used for personal ornamentation, especially one made of precious metals and stones; a piece of jewellery."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bejewel; to decorate or bedeck with jewels or gems."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jewel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Platycypha caligata","blocks":[{"text":"Platycypha caligata, the dancing jewel, is a species of damselfly in the family Chlorocyphidae. It is found in eastern, central and southern Africa from Ethiopia to Angola and South Africa. Its natural habitats include shady parts of subtropical or tropical streams and rivers in forest, woodland, savanna, and shrubland, and shorelines of lakes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Platycypha_caligata.jpg/330px-Platycypha_caligata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platycypha_caligata"},{"title":"Jewel (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Jewel Kilcher is an American singer-songwriter. She has been nominated for four Grammy Awards and has sold over 30 million albums worldwide as of 2024."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Jewel20220730.jpg/330px-Jewel20220730.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewel_(singer)"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_Jewel_%28Platycypha_caligata%29_teneral_male.jpg/500px-Dancing_Jewel_%28Platycypha_caligata%29_teneral_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_Jewel_%28Platycypha_caligata%29_teneral_male.jpg/1280px-Dancing_Jewel_%28Platycypha_caligata%29_teneral_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Dancing_Jewel_%28Platycypha_caligata%29_teneral_male.jpg/500px-Dancing_Jewel_%28Platycypha_caligata%29_teneral_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADancing_Jewel_(Platycypha_caligata)_teneral_male.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Platycypha_caligata_female.jpg/330px-Platycypha_caligata_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7a/Platycypha_caligata_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Platycypha_caligata_female.jpg/330px-Platycypha_caligata_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"